From: CoolFreeze23 <34906576+CoolFreeze23@users.noreply.github.com>
Date: Tue, 20 Oct 2026 12:00:00 +0900
Subject: [PATCH] wifi: ath12k: forget a deleted TID queue in peer tid cleanup

ath12k_dp_rx_peer_tid_cleanup() hands every active TID queue to its
pending delete element, which frees the descriptor once REO has flushed
it. The TID stays marked active in rx_tid_active_bitmask, and
dp_peer->reoq_bufs[tid] and rx_tid->qbuf keep pointing at the
descriptor.

Two paths then give the soon-to-be-freed descriptor back to the
hardware:

- dp_peer outlives the link peer of an MLO station. When a new primary
  link sets the TID up, ath12k_dp_rx_assign_reoq() finds
  reoq_bufs[tid] still set and reuses it.
- A peer whose DP state is cleaned up and set up again keeps the active
  bit, so the next ADDBA takes the "already set up" branch and
  re-programs the queue into REO (UPDATE_RX_QUEUE) and, on IPQ5332,
  into firmware (WMI_PEER_REORDER_QUEUE_SETUP).

After the free, REO writes into a recycled kmalloc-2k object. For each
TID that was active, clear its active bit and forget both copies of the
descriptor once it belongs to the delete element.
---
diff --git a/drivers/net/wireless/ath/ath12k/dp_rx.c b/drivers/net/wireless/ath/ath12k/dp_rx.c
--- a/drivers/net/wireless/ath/ath12k/dp_rx.c
+++ b/drivers/net/wireless/ath/ath12k/dp_rx.c
@@ -724,11 +724,28 @@ void ath12k_dp_rx_peer_tid_cleanup(struc
 		return;
 
 	for (i = 0; i <= IEEE80211_NUM_TIDS; i++) {
+		bool was_active = peer->rx_tid_active_bitmask & BIT(i);
+
 		rx_tid = &peer->dp_peer->rx_tid[i];
 
 		ath12k_dp_arch_rx_peer_tid_delete(dp, peer, i);
 		ath12k_dp_arch_rx_frags_cleanup(dp, rx_tid, true);
 
+		/*
+		 * An active TID's queue descriptor now belongs to the pending
+		 * delete element, which frees it once REO has flushed it.
+		 * dp_peer outlives this link peer for an MLO station (a new
+		 * primary link can set the TID up again), so forget the
+		 * descriptor here: otherwise ath12k_dp_rx_assign_reoq() would
+		 * hand the soon-to-be-freed buffer to REO again.
+		 */
+		if (was_active) {
+			peer->rx_tid_active_bitmask &= ~BIT(i);
+			memset(&peer->dp_peer->reoq_bufs[i], 0,
+			       sizeof(peer->dp_peer->reoq_bufs[i]));
+			memset(&rx_tid->qbuf, 0, sizeof(rx_tid->qbuf));
+		}
+
 		spin_unlock_bh(&dp->dp_lock);
 		timer_delete_sync(&rx_tid->frag_timer);
 		spin_lock_bh(&dp->dp_lock);
